ation","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Albertine-Rift birding + biodiversity","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"300+ birds with 29 Albertine-Rift endemics and 13 primate species on the Congo–Nile divide","si":"deepdive","blurb":"300+ birds with 29 Albertine-Rift endemics and 13 primate species on the Congo–Nile divide","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","commission":"DMC/specialist","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["deepdive"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A One&Only Nyungwe House honeymoon","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$1,000-3,000+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 2-5 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"a tea-estate-set forest retreat — glass-walled suites over the canopy, a spa, private guiding and the forest at the door","si":"ultra","blurb":"a tea-estate-set forest retreat — glass-walled suites over the canopy, a spa, private guiding and the forest at the door","when":"standing; peak 2-5 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","romance","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"evidenced","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A tea-estate + forest-wellness day","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$20-80/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the emerald tea plantations that ring Nyungwe, a plucking-and-tasting visit, and the forest''s own serenity — a gentle, restorative counterpoint to the trekking","si":"culture","blurb":"the emerald tea plantations that ring Nyungwe, a plucking-and-tasting visit, and the forest''s own serenity — a gentle, restorative counterpoint to the trekking","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","commission":"DMC/community","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture","wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","ultra":"destination","wellness":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_basis":"the dossier''s own SI block filed this jewel under a heading resolving to ''wellness'' via ruled RULES. Not a keyword match on the jewel text."},{"name":"A Nyungwe forest honeymoon","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a tea-estate-set forest retreat — glass-walled suites over the canopy, a spa, private guiding and the forest at the door","si":"romance","blurb":"a tea-estate-set forest retreat — glass-walled suites over the canopy, a spa, private guiding and the forest at the door","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"evidenced","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Nyungwe?","a":"The trek and the health advisory - not crime. Chimp trekking is a strenuous 2-6-hour hike over steep, slippery montane slopes (good boots + fitness), and the canopy walkway sways 70 m up (a head-for-heights helps). Malaria is present (prophylaxis + DEET, lower at altitude), and it''s remote - carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How much is chimp trekking, and how does it compare to gorillas?","a":"The chimp permit is $250 (vs Rwanda''s $1,500 gorilla permit) - a more affordable, more active primate trek: faster-moving chimps, a 2-6-hour hike, a one-hour encounter (7-8 m distance, a face mask, an armed ranger). It pairs beautifully with the gorillas of Volcanoes.","source":"greatadventuresafaris.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"What else is there besides chimps at Nyungwe?","a":"Plenty: the canopy walk ($60), huge colobus troops (up to 400), the Isumo waterfall hike ($15), world-class birding (29 Albertine-Rift endemics), and tea plantations on the forest edge - Nyungwe rewards a 2-3-day stay.","source":"nyungweforestnationalpark.org","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Nyungwe?","a":"For hiking, the canopy walk and general primates, come in the drier Jun-Sep and Dec-Feb (firmer trails); for chimp trekking, the wetter Oct-May can be better (abundant fruit keeps chimps lower and closer).","source":"safaris-uganda.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Rwanda?","a":"Visa on arrival $30 (or online via Irembo); passport valid 6 months. Yellow fever is required only if arriving from a YF-endemic country (not direct from the US).","source":"thingstodoinrwanda.com","si_tag":"globaladv"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Nyungwe Forest Guide: Chimpanzee Trekking, the Canopy Walk, Permits & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan a Nyungwe Forest trip - Rwanda''s ancient montane rainforest: chimpanzee trekking ($250), East Africa''s first canopy walkway (70 m up), colobus troops up to 400, the Isumo waterfall hike and world-class Albertine-Rift birding - with the FCDO advisory, fitness and cost, and the 3-park Rwanda circuit.","slug":"nyungwe-forest-rwanda","primary_keyword":"Nyungwe Forest chimpanzee trekking","long_tail":["Nyungwe chimpanzee permit cost 2026","Nyungwe canopy walk","colobus monkeys Nyungwe","Nyungwe waterfall hike","Nyungwe vs Volcanoes","is Nyungwe safe","Nyungwe birding Albertine Rift"],"search_language":"fr","local_keywords":["Nyungwe","inguge","canopy walk","colobus","Isumo","Gisakura","Albertine Rift"],"hreflang":["en","fr"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-01","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-01","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:58Z","source_updated":"2026-06-10T15:14:19+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["reconsider-travel","regional-ebola-alert"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"was). Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; per the safari-build rule the chimp trek is globaladv (PRIMARY here) - safari (big-game) is a documented MISS on a montane forest; canopy walk + waterfall hikes = globaladv; birding/biodiversity = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"chimp trekking + canopy walk + colobus + waterfall hikes (PRIMARY)"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"One&Only Nyungwe House"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"Albertine-Rift biodiversity / birding"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future","note":"tea communities"}],"ultra":[{"name":"One&Only Nyungwe House - the forest''s apex stay","why_ultra":"glass-walled suites on a tea estate at the forest edge, a spa, and private guiding to the chimps + canopy walk","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,500-3,000+/night"},{"name":"A private chimp + canopy + colobus + birding week","why_ultra":"an exclusive-guide forest immersion: two chimp treks, the canopy walk, colobus, the waterfall hike + specialist birding, from an ultra lodge","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"The 3-park luxury Rwanda circuit (Volcanoes + Nyungwe + Akagera)","why_ultra":"gorillas + chimps/canopy walk + the Big-Five savanna, private-guided - and it unlocks the Nov-May 30% gorilla-permit discount","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Nyungwe Forest National Park, Rwanda"},"geo":{"lat":-2.5,"lng":29.2},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["akagera-np-rwanda","volcanoes-national-park-rwanda"]}'::jsonb, 15),
  ('queen-elizabeth-np-uganda', '05A', 'Queen Elizabeth National Park', 'Uganda', 'Tree-climbing lions, a hippo-thronged channel and 600 birds', 'live', 'verified', 'lion', 'Uganda — Queen Elizabeth / Rift Valley', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["CONTENT-ONLY, no Book path, no waiver. DYNAMIC - re-verify each cycle, flip to live when it clears. Redirect safari demand to Kenya/Tanzania/Akagera","Uganda''s most popular savanna park (~1,978 km2, est. 1952 as Kazinga NP, renamed for Queen Elizabeth II): 95+ mammals and 600+ birds - the country''s most biodiverse safari","The tree-climbing lions of Ishasha (lions in fig/acacia trees - rare behaviour); the Kazinga Channel (40km, Lakes Edward<->George; UWA boat $30 - hippos/crocs/elephants/birds); Kyambura Gorge chimps (all latent while held)","Western edge borders Virunga (DR Congo) - a separate STANDING security concern even apart from the Ebola","Park fee $40 (24h); yellow fever MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe); eVisa (no visa-on-arrival); malaria in all regions (prophylaxis) - all latent while held","Live twins = Kenya (Maasai Mara/Amboseli), Tanzania (Serengeti), akagera-np-rwanda (Rwanda Big Five). Anchors the Uganda cluster with bwindi/murchison-falls/kibale"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Kasese/Mbarara/Kampala (all latent while held)","malaria":"present in all regions - prophylaxis (latent while held)","yellow_fever":"MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe, >=10 days before)","ebola":"Sudan virus outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17 - the dominant, disqualifying hazard","drc_border":"western edge borders Virunga (DR Congo) - separate standing security concern; when live, keep to eastern/central sectors","activity_note":"HEALTH-SPINE DOMINANT: Ebola outbreak is the hazard. FCDO BASIS (gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda, read 2026-08-20): health screening on arrival and departure; Ugandan border with the DRC closed from 27 May per the National Task Force; the UK Returning Workers Scheme activated due to the outbreak. NOTE THE FCDO ADVISES AGAINST NO TRAVEL TO UGANDA - posture 1 - so any book-suppression here is OUR health judgement, not an advisory one, and is DAVID''S CALL - CONTENT-ONLY, Book suppressed, no waiver, redirect to Kenya/Tanzania/Akagera. DYNAMIC - re-verify each cycle. Safari/boat + malaria hazards + the DRC border are secondary/standing and moot for booking while held. When reopened: standard game-drive/boat rules, keep back from hippos/crocs, ranger-guided","booking_hold":false,"fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda","read":"2026-09-04T12:02:58Z","page_updated":"2026-09-02T16:45:31+01:00","source_country":"uganda","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed","posture_basis":"alert_status empty; quoted sentences name another country","posture_corrected":"2026-08-23 - was AREA-RESTRICTED, derived from prose about a neighbour"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"latent_peak":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb (drier - game at water, firmer tracks) - IF cleared","latent_green":"Mar-May + Oct-Nov (rains, lush/birdy, softer rates)","latent_booking_lead":"lodges 2-4 mo peak - NOT applicable while held","reverify_trigger":"check Uganda''s advisory EVERY publish cycle - DYNAMIC health advisory; re-verify western DRC/Virunga line before live routing","redirect":"live safari demand -> Kenya (Maasai Mara/Amboseli) / Tanzania (Serengeti) / akagera-np-rwanda (Rwanda Big Five)"},"jewels":[{"name":"The tree-climbing lions of Ishasha","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD; latent Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":null,"hook":"one of only a couple of places on Earth where lions habitually lounge in fig and acacia trees","si":"safari","blurb":"one of only a couple of places on Earth where lions habitually lounge in fig and acacia trees","when":"HELD; latent Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"evidenced","deepdive":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The Kazinga Channel boat cruise","status":"held","tier":"essential","price_band":"HELD (UWA boat $30 latent)","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"a 40-km natural channel between Lakes Edward and George","si":"adventure","blurb":"a 40-km natural channel between Lakes Edward and George","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","source":"https://www.gorillasafariscompany.com/2024/03/06/how-much-is-the-kazinga-channel-boat-cruise-in-2024-2025/","accessed":"2026-08-01","source_carried":true,"source_basis":"carried from the dossier lane source; the proper noun ''The Kazinga Channel'' from the jewel name appears in the URL. NOT a human read of the jewel."},{"name":"Kyambura Gorge chimpanzee trek","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"a sunken \"valley of apes\" — a forested gorge in the savanna holding a habituated chimp community; a globaladv trek unique to Queen Elizabeth","si":"adventure","blurb":"a sunken \"valley of apes\" — a forested gorge in the savanna holding a habituated chimp community; a globaladv trek unique to Queen Elizabeth","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A 600-bird birder''s grail","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Uganda''s most bird-rich park — 600+ species across savanna, wetland, forest and lake habitats, from shoebill-country wetlands to Kazinga''s pelicans and skimmers","si":"deepdive","blurb":"Uganda''s most bird-rich park — 600+ species across savanna, wetland, forest and lake habitats, from shoebill-country wetlands to Kazinga''s pelicans and skimmers","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["deepdive","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"primary","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Rift-Valley safari-lodge honeymoon (held)","status":"held","tier":"comfort","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Mweya Safari Lodge on its channel-side peninsula, Ishasha Wilderness Camp, Kyambura Gorge Lodge — crater-lake and channel luxury after the game drive","si":"ultra","blurb":"Mweya Safari Lodge on its channel-side peninsula, Ishasha Wilderness Camp, Kyambura Gorge Lodge — crater-lake and channel luxury after the game drive","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)","wells":["stay","move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["safari","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where can I go on safari instead, right now?","a":"Kenya (Maasai Mara / Amboseli,, bookable) or Tanzania (Serengeti / Ngorongoro,, bookable) for the classic Big-game plains - or Akagera, Rwanda (US, a Big-Five comeback ~2h from Kigali) for the nearest live savanna. We route all Uganda safari demand there.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Will this clear - should I wait for Queen Elizabeth?","a":"Possibly - this is a health-driven, dynamic advisory (an outbreak, not conflict), so it can be lifted when the outbreak is contained. For a firm 2026 safari, book Kenya, Tanzania or Akagera now.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would Queen Elizabeth offer when it reopens?","a":"Uganda''s most popular savanna - the tree-climbing lions of Ishasha, the Kazinga Channel boat cruise (hippos, crocs, elephants, 600+ birds), Kyambura Gorge chimps, and a Rift-Valley backdrop of crater lakes. All held until the advisory lifts.","source":"ugandawildlife.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Is the DRC border a concern too?","a":"Yes - separately. The park''s western edge borders Virunga in the DR Congo, a standing security concern in its own right; when the park is live, itineraries keep to the eastern/central sectors. **FCDO travel advice for Uganda:** the FCDO names no advisory against travel to Uganda. *https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda — page updated 2026-07-27.*","source":"national-parks.org","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are the non-Ebola health requirements for Uganda?","a":"Yellow fever is mandatory for entry (all travelers >=1 yr, checked at Entebbe, vaccinate >=10 days before); malaria prophylaxis is essential (all regions); carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_description":"What it is, why it''s held, and where to safari instead (Kenya, Tanzania, Rwanda''s Akagera).","slug":"queen-elizabeth-np-uganda","primary_keyword":"Queen Elizabeth National Park tree-climbing lions","long_tail":["Kazinga Channel boat cruise","Ishasha tree-climbing 