"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"held","note":"600+ birds - birder''s grail"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Kyambura Gorge Lodge / Mweya Safari Lodge (HELD)","why_ultra":"the park''s apex stays - a converted coffee store above the chimp gorge and a channel-side peninsula lodge; documented for the day the hold lifts, sold by no one today","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"},{"name":"A private Ishasha + Kazinga + Kyambura week (HELD)","why_ultra":"tree-climbing lions + the channel boat + the chimp gorge + the crater lakes, privately guided - latent","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Queen Elizabeth National Park, Uganda"},"geo":{"lat":-0.2,"lng":30},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["bwindi-impenetrable-uganda","kibale-forest-uganda","murchison-falls-uganda"]}'::jsonb, 16),
  ('ruaha-tanzania', '05A', 'Ruaha National Park', 'Tanzania', 'One in ten of the world''s lions, wild dogs', 'live', 'verified', 'lion', 'Tanzania — Southern Circuit / Ruaha', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Tanzania''s largest national park (~20,226 km2) and a global lion stronghold - an estimated ~10% of the world''s lions, in some of the largest prides ever recorded (hunt buffalo and even giraffe)","One of East Africa''s best wild-dog destinations - within the 3rd-largest wild-dog population in the world; ~12,000 elephants in the greater ecosystem; a rare East-meets-Southern-Africa transition zone (greater + lesser kudu, sable, roan)","The Great Ruaha River is the dry-season lifeline and focus of game viewing; 570+ birds; remote, uncrowded, mainly fly-in (south-central Tanzania, ~130 km west of Iringa)","disclose LGBTQ+ targeting; travel with a licensed operator","Best Jun-Oct (dry - game on the river); green season Nov-Apr lush/birdy (some camps close); Ruaha''s signature is the walking safari (+ night drives + fly-camping); no rhino (poached out - four of Big Five)","Sold via Tanzanian safari DMCs + camp consortia 10-20%+ - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; light-aircraft fly-in + TANAPA park fees are pass-through; TZS (~2,633/USD, USD is the safari currency); eVisa; AMREF evac essential (remote interior)"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 999","hospital":"Remote deep-interior - medical access by air; AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance essential; nearest referral Iringa/Dar","malaria":"present (interior park) - prophylaxis + DEET advised","yellow_fever":"not required direct from US/Europe; mandatory if transiting >12h through a risk country (e.g. Kenya)","activity_note":"disclose LGBTQ+ targeting - same-sex relations criminalized; travel with a licensed operator). Ruaha is a remote fly-in wilderness - AMREF evac + insurance are load-bearing. Walking safari only with armed ranger (single file, downwind, no bright colors); predator-dense driving (keep still/quiet, never on foot near a kill); night drives to vehicle rules","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-09-01T16:20:26Z","page_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00","source_country":"tanzania","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct (dry) - game concentrates on the Great Ruaha River; the premier predator season; book 4-8 mo ahead (few camps)","shoulder":"Nov + late Oct (good rates, softer crowds)","green":"Dec-Apr (rains - lush, superb birding, cheapest; some camps close, roads soften)","booking_lead":"premium camps 4-8 mo for Jun-Oct (limited beds); green 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"green-season birding + big-cat cubs (Dec-Apr); the southern-circuit combo (Ruaha + Nyerere/Selous) as an uncrowded alternative to the north","event_peaks":"Jul-Oct + Christmas/NY; the dry-season predator spectacle","fire_date":"Jun-Oct 6-9 mo out (beds scarce); the Ruaha + Nyerere southern-circuit combo by prior Aug-Oct; position as the connoisseur''s uncrowded predator safari for northern-circuit returnees"},"jewels":[{"name":"The lion kingdom","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct peak","draw_rank":1,"hook":"an estimated one in ten of the world''s lions live in Ruaha, in some of the largest prides ever recorded","si":"safari","blurb":"an estimated one in ten of the world''s lions live in Ruaha, in some of the largest prides ever recorded","when":"Jun-Oct peak","commission":"DMC/camp","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Wild dogs + a transition-zone roster","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"one of the world''s best wild-dog strongholds, plus a rare East-meets-Southern-Africa game list — greater and lesser kudu, sable, roan","si":"safari","blurb":"one of the world''s best wild-dog strongholds, plus a rare East-meets-Southern-Africa game list — greater and lesser kudu, sable, roan","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/camp","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Walking safari + fly-camping + night drives","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$60-500/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Ruaha is one of Tanzania''s great walking-safari parks","si":"adventure","blurb":"Ruaha is one of Tanzania''s great walking-safari parks","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Predator research + transition-zone biodiversity","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Ruaha is a hub of lion and wild-dog conservation science in a globally significant ecosystem, plus a 570-bird list","si":"deepdive","blurb":"Ruaha is a hub of lion and wild-dog conservation science in a globally significant ecosystem, plus a 570-bird list","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/specialist","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["deepdive"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Jabali Ridge / Mwagusi honeymoon","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$900-2,500+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Asilia''s Jabali Ridge tucked into a kopje above the plains, or Mwagusi''s legendary bush bandas on a sand river","si":"ultra","blurb":"Asilia''s Jabali Ridge tucked into a kopje above the plains, or Mwagusi''s legendary bush bandas on a sand river","when":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance","safari","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Ruaha wilderness honeymoon","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"consortia/host","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Ruaha?","a":"Not the parks - the advisory''s concerns are the far-southeastern Mtwara Region (terrorism, far away) and city petty crime, plus a flagged LGBTQ+ targeting concern travelers should weigh (Tanzanian law criminalizes same-sex relations). In Ruaha itself the risks are ordinary safari ones plus remoteness - it''s a fly-in wilderness, so carry AMREF evac + insurance and follow the walking-safari rules.","source":"newsweek.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why choose Ruaha over the northern circuit?","a":"For wildness and predators without the crowds - ~10% of the world''s lions in huge prides, one of the world''s best wild-dog populations, big elephant herds and a transition-zone game roster, all in Tanzania''s largest park with a fraction of the vehicles. It''s the connoisseur''s safari, best paired with Nyerere/Selous.","source":"national-parks.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Ruaha?","a":"The dry season, Jun-Oct, when the Great Ruaha River becomes the only water and game - lions, dogs, elephants - concentrates dramatically along it; the green season (Nov-Apr) is lush and superb for birds (570+ species) but some camps close and roads soften.","source":"getsafaritours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How do I get to Ruaha, and how long should I stay?","a":"Mostly by light-aircraft fly-in (from Dar, Iringa or as part of a southern-circuit hop); give it 3-4 nights to justify the flight and to do the river drives and a walking safari - it''s not a day-trip park.","source":"getsafaritours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Tanzania?","a":"eVisa required - apply on the official portal before departure. Yellow fever is not required direct from the US/Europe, but is mandatory if you transit >12 h through a risk country like Kenya.","source":"tanzania-specialist.com","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ruaha National Park Guide: Lions, Wild Dogs, Walking Safaris & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan a Ruaha safari - Tanzania''s largest, wildest and least-crowded park: ~10% of the world''s lions in record prides, one of the world''s best wild-dog populations, walking safaris and the Great Ruaha River - with the FCDO advisory, best time (Jun-Oct), the fly-in and where to stay on the southern circuit.","slug":"ruaha-tanzania","primary_keyword":"Ruaha National Park safari","long_tail":["Ruaha lions prides","Ruaha wild dogs","Ruaha walking safari","Ruaha vs Serengeti","is Tanzania safe safari","Ruaha best time to visit","southern circuit Tanzania"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Ruaha","simba","mbwa mwitu","tembo","mto"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-01","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-01","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:17Z","source_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["reconsider-travel","mtwara-terrorism-carveout-far","lgbtq-targeting"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"also disclose the LGBTQ+ targeting consideration (same-sex relations criminalized). Travel with a licensed operator; remote fly-in - AMREF evac essential. Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; per the safari-build rule big game/predators is safari (PRIMARY here - lion + wild-dog stronghold), NOT globaladv; walking safari + night drive + fly-camping = globaladv; predator research + transition-zone biodiversity + 570 birds = deepdive; no rhino - poached out (four of Big Five); sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"big-game/predators - ~10% of the world''s lions + a wild-dog stronghold (PRIMARY)"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"walking safari + night drive + fly-camping"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"Jabali Ridge / Mwagusi"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"predator research / transition-zone biodiversity / 570 birds"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Jabali Ridge (Asilia) / Mwagusi - the wilderness-luxury apex","why_ultra":"a kopje-set design lodge and a legendary sand-river camp, deep in Tanzania''s largest park, with walking safaris and private guiding","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,200-2,500+/night"},{"name":"A private lion-and-wild-dog walking week","why_ultra":"an exclusive-guide safari: river drives for the great prides + walking safaris + a fly-camp night + wild-dog tracking, from an ultra camp","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"The private southern-circuit safari (Ruaha + Nyerere/Selous)","why_ultra":"Tanzania''s wild south flown and privately guided: Ruaha''s predators + Nyerere''s Rufiji boat safaris, far from the northern crowds","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Ruaha National Park, Tanzania"},"geo":{"lat":-7.7,"lng":34.8333},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":["lake-manyara-tanzania","ngorongoro-crater-tanzania","nyerere-selous-tanzania","serengeti-tanzania","tarangire-tanzania"]}'::jsonb, 17)
insert into public.destinations (id, region_code, name, country, line, status, depth, img, sub_region, si, feel, tier_range, price_band, draw_rank, data, position) values
  ('samburu-kenya', '05A', 'Samburu National Reserve', 'Kenya', 'Northern Kenya''s wild frontier', 'live', 'verified', 'safariJeep', 'Kenya — Samburu / Northern Frontier', '{"safari","ultra","romance","adventure","deepdive","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["The ''Samburu Special Five'' - Grevy''s zebra (80%+ of the world''s remaining), reticulated giraffe, Beisa oryx, gerenuk, Somali ostrich - arid-country species found ONLY in Kenya''s northern reserves, not the southern parks","~900 elephants + some of Kenya''s best leopard (riverine forest of the Ewaso Ng''iro River); far fewer vehicles than the south - the connoisseur''s Kenya","The Born Free legacy - George + Joy Adamson raised Elsa the lioness here; home of the proud Samburu people (cousins of the Maasai)","ROUTE VIA FLY-IN","Best Jul-Sep + Jan-Feb (dry); 2-3 days ideal, pairs with Laikipia (rhino); sold via Kenya safari DMCs 10-25% - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation","KES (~129/USD) + M-Pesa but safari quoted USD; eTA required; malaria prophylaxis advised (chloroquine-resistant); YF only if arriving from a risk country; AMREF Flying Doctors for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112 / 911 (limited response in the remote north); Kenya Red Cross ambulance 1199; AMREF Flying Doctors for bush evac","hospital":"Remote north - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Nanyuki/Nairobi","malaria":"prophylaxis advised (Samburu qualifies, chloroquine-resistant); DEET at dusk","yellow_fever":"compulsory only if arriving from a risk country; CDC recommends for most","activity_note":"route via fly-in, verify current advisory). Dangerous game at close range - stay in the vehicle, follow the guide; camel/bush walks with armed guides. Remote north - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:02Z","page_updated":"2026-09-01T12:05:48+01:00","source_country":"kenya","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"Mandera, Wajir and Garissa counties","lvl":4,"note":"The Somalia border counties."},{"name":"Lamu County","lvl":4},{"name":"Tana River","lvl":4},{"name":"Kilifi north of Malindi","lvl":4},{"name":"The northern border areas","lvl":4},{"name":"Eastleigh, Nairobi","lvl":3},{"name":"Kibera, Nairobi","lvl":3}]},"timing":{"peak":"Jul-Sep (dry, hot, wildlife on the river) + Jan-Feb (dry)","shoulder":"Jun + Oct (good game, softer rates)","green":"Mar-May + Nov (rains - lush, birdlife, quietest, cheapest)","booking_lead":"river lodges + fly-in 3-6 mo (Jul-Sep + Jan-Feb; distinctive lodges are small); shoulder 2-4 mo; green 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"green-season value + birding; combine Laikipia (rhino) an hour away, or Mara/Amboseli","event_peaks":"Jul-Sep + Christmas/NY + Easter","fire_date":"Jul-Sep + Jan-Feb Special-Five safaris 4-6 mo out; green birding value by prior Sep-Oct; bundle Samburu + Laikipia (northern-Kenya pairing)"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Samburu Special Five","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$500-2,000/pp/day","timing":"Jul-Sep + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Grevy''s zebra, reticulated giraffe, gerenuk, Beisa oryx and Somali ostrich — arid-country species you won''t see in the southern parks","si":"safari","blurb":"Grevy''s zebra, reticulated giraffe, gerenuk, Beisa oryx and Somali ostrich — arid-country species you won''t see in the southern parks","when":"Jul-Sep + Jan-Feb","commission":"safari DMC 10-25%","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["safari"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"destination","safari":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":25,"commission_